                <pb facs="0760" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 215.11 V 28/4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister McCreery.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department is in receipt of your
                    dispatch, No. 41, of the 19th ultimo, with which you inclose copies of notes
                    exchanged with the foreign office of Honduras, from which it appears that the
                    Government of Honduras will issue the necessary orders for the arrest of Charles
                    Vandenberg, alias Carl Nicklas, whose extradition to answer the charge of
                    forgery committed in the State of New York is desired.</p>
                <p>The department is gratified at the action of the Government of Honduras in this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>Copies of your dispatch and of its inclosures have been sent to the governor of
                    New York for his information.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
